# Deploy after security work

When adding or changing **security** (headers, CSP, auth, cookies, secrets handling, XSS/safe hrefs, Prisma/server-only, rate limits, API hardening, etc.):

1. Stage only intentional files when the user asks to commit — **never** commit `.env` or real secrets.
2. Prefer commit message style `security: …` when the user asks to commit.
3. **Do not** `git push` unless the user explicitly asks to push (see `no-auto-push`).

If the user asks to push and it fails (auth/network), report the error and what remains to do locally.

When security work is done and ready, briefly tell the user it is ready to commit/push — do not run those commands unprompted.
